course: dictionary
lesson: 2181
title: Corundum, a very hard mineral
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mineral is a natural solid found in rocks and the ground. Some minerals are so hard that they can scratch almost anything. Corundum is one of these hard minerals, and the sentences around it give you clues about what it is.
explain: «Rubies and sapphires are the same mineral, corundum; red corundum is ruby, and other colours are sapphire.» The words after the semicolon explain the first part. A ruby is a red kind of corundum, and a sapphire is a coloured kind, such as blue.
explain: «Tiny traces of other elements, such as chromium in ruby, give corundum its colour.» Traces means very small amounts. So a tiny bit of another element changes the colour of the same mineral. Swap in your own meaning to check it still makes sense.
fact: Corundum is a very hard natural mineral made of aluminium oxide.
fact: Rubies and sapphires are coloured kinds of corundum.
fact: Corundum scores 9 on the Mohs scale of hardness, second only to diamond, which scores 10.
fact: Because corundum is so hard, crushed corundum is used to make sandpaper and grinding tools, called emery.
fact: Red corundum is ruby; blue and other colours are sapphire.
exercise: «Rubies and sapphires are the same mineral, corundum.» What is corundum? | A coloured sweet | A type of glass made in a factory | A soft metal used for jewellery | *A very hard natural mineral made of aluminium oxide
exercise: Red corundum is called ruby. What is blue corundum called? | Chromium | *Sapphire | Diamond | Emery
exercise: Corundum scores 9 on the Mohs scale of hardness. Which mineral is only above it? | Ruby | Sandpaper | *Diamond | Chromium
test: «Tiny traces of other elements, such as chromium in ruby, give corundum its colour.» What does traces mean here? | Painted lines | Hidden treasure | *Very small amounts | Large heaps
test: Why is crushed corundum used to make sandpaper? | Because it is red | Because it is soft and smooth | *Because it is very hard | Because it tastes sweet
exam: «Rubies and sapphires are one mineral, corundum, and a pinch of another element decides the colour.» What decides the colour? | *A pinch of another element | The shape of the stone | The size of the stone | The water in the rock
